["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The US Treasury Secretary Threatens Allies with Divine Wrath, and Proves He Has No Cards Treasury Secretary Bessent paints America as an irritable god and demands allies submit like Pascal&#x27;s wager. Farrell sees through the op-ed: the louder the threat, the more it proves the US has no means to deliver, and allies have already started hedging. Hidden Forces Hidden Forces Bessent&#x27;s Wager and Why the World is Calling America&#x27;s Bluff | Henry Farrell Trade War Dollar System Geopolitics US Institutions Financial Sanctions Pascal&#x27;s wager weaponized interdependence flexible realism unitary executive neo-royalism busted flush\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-hiddenforces-美国财长用神罚威胁盟国-反而证明手里没牌/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2b4203c8f6331570-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"H\"><span class=\"dur\">51:39</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Hidden Forces</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The US Treasury Secretary Threatens Allies with Divine Wrath, and Proves He Has No Cards</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Treasury Secretary Bessent paints America as an irritable god and demands allies submit like Pascal&#x27;s wager. Farrell sees through the op-ed: the louder the threat, the more it proves the US has no means to deliver, and allies have already started hedging.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Trade War</span><span class=\"tag\">Dollar System</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Consciousness Has No Finish Line: The Brain Is Multiple Drafts, Not a Screening Room Dennett argues against the &quot;Cartesian Theater&quot;: there is no single finish line where all sensations converge into consciousness; the brain is parallel discriminations, multiple drafts that never get pooled, and even &quot;when did you become aware&quot; often has no factual answer. The Partially Examined Life Partially Examined Life Ep. 399: Dan Dennett&#x27;s Model of Mind (Part One) Consciousness Philosophy Models of Mind Multiple Drafts Cognitive Science Cartesian Theater Multiple Drafts Model Phi phenomenon Qualia Homunculus Stalinesque vs. Orwellian\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-pel-笛卡尔剧场不存在-意识不是放映-而是多重草稿/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/5a66360fe1170966-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">47:34</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Partially Examined Life</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Consciousness Has No Finish Line: The Brain Is Multiple Drafts, Not a Screening Room</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Dennett argues against the &quot;Cartesian Theater&quot;: there is no single finish line where all sensations converge into consciousness; the brain is parallel discriminations, multiple drafts that never get pooled, and even &quot;when did you become aware&quot; often has no factual answer.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Consciousness</span><span class=\"tag\">Philosophy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"The hard part of dementia care isn&#x27;t the patient — it&#x27;s the caregiver who gets ground down The hard part of dementia care isn&#x27;t the illness itself, but the caregiver worn down day after day — care turns a wife into a nurse and pushes a millennial to quit. Love is the starting point, not the support, and the system hasn&#x27;t caught these families yet. 不合时宜 不合时宜 漫长的告别：失智症、照护者与终将老去的我们 Dementia Eldercare Caregivers Long-term care insurance Aging Only children Hogeweyk The Soul of Care informal care long-term care insurance wet-on-wet watercolor\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-cn300980-失智照护的难不在失智老人-而在会被拖垮的照护者/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/bda8c0f9bba83da6-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"不\"><span class=\"dur\">1:04:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">不合时宜</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The hard part of dementia care isn&#x27;t the patient — it&#x27;s the caregiver who gets ground down</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The hard part of dementia care isn&#x27;t the illness itself, but the caregiver worn down day after day — care turns a wife into a nurse and pushes a millennial to quit. Love is the starting point, not the support, and the system hasn&#x27;t caught these families yet.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Dementia</span><span class=\"tag\">Eldercare</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"The fab bottleneck isn&#x27;t the lithography tool, it&#x27;s the OHT cars on the ceiling What really caps wafer fab capacity isn&#x27;t just the lithography tool, but the OHT cars running back and forth on the ceiling. The 300mm transition made them mandatory, and today the market is a Daifuku-Muratec duopoly. Asianometry Asianometry The Little Ceiling Robots Inside a Semiconductor Fab AMHS OHT Semiconductor manufacturing Wafer fabs Automated logistics Equipment monopoly AMHS / Automated Material Handling System FOUP / Front Opening Unified Pod OHT / Overhead Hoist Transport Stocker Interbay / Intrabay\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-asianometry-别只盯着光刻机-天花板上的-oht-小车也在卡产能/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/c6301489e9b3f727-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">20:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The fab bottleneck isn&#x27;t the lithography tool, it&#x27;s the OHT cars on the ceiling</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">What really caps wafer fab capacity isn&#x27;t just the lithography tool, but the OHT cars running back and forth on the ceiling. The 300mm transition made them mandatory, and today the market is a Daifuku-Muratec duopoly.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AMHS</span><span class=\"tag\">OHT</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The Treasury Secretary Trades the Bond Market Like a Position, and Prices Will Win US Treasury Secretary Bessent is intervening in the bond market, trade and sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep pushing prices up, and his strategy may come to nothing. Patrick Boyle Patrick Boyle Scott Bessent Is at War With Prices — and Prices Are Winning! Treasury bonds Fiscal policy Inflation Federal Reserve Crypto Trade war TGA (Treasury General Account) On-the-run vs off-the-run bonds Duration neutral Term premium Stablecoin\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-patrickboyle-贝森特与价格的战争-财政部长的宏观赌局/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2eb71149af422d0e-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">44:51</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Patrick Boyle</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The Treasury Secretary Trades the Bond Market Like a Position, and Prices Will Win</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">US Treasury Secretary Bessent is intervening in the bond market, trade and sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep pushing prices up, and his strategy may come to nothing.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Treasury bonds</span><span class=\"tag\">Fiscal policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Elite Universities Are a Cartel: They Sell Status, Not Education America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brand by freezing enrollment, running alumni donations, and absorbing federal research grants; they sell status, not education. Modern MBA Modern MBA The American College Cartel University Finance Endowments Elite Education Admissions US Innovation endowment advancement provost tenure yield tech tree\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-modernmba-精英大学是制造稀缺的卡特尔-而非教育机构/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3676f3a101faa05c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"M\"><span class=\"dur\">45:11</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Modern MBA</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Elite Universities Are a Cartel: They Sell Status, Not Education</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brand by freezing enrollment, running alumni donations, and absorbing federal research grants; they sell status, not education.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">University Finance</span><span class=\"tag\">Endowments</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Phage Bets Its Future on 10,000-Fold Reversion, and the First Humanized EBV Antibody Phages hedge their bets through 10,000-fold reversion mutations in SSRs, humanized EBV antibodies block tumors in vivo, and vaccine efforts advance on multiple fronts. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1353: Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies Phage Bet-hedging EBV Antibodies Vaccines Cognitive laziness SSR / simple sequence repeat bet-hedging contingency locus hybridoma\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-twiv-噬菌体用随机突变下注-ebv人类抗体首次成功/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">1:52:21</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Phage Bets Its Future on 10,000-Fold Reversion, and the First Humanized EBV Antibody</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Phages hedge their bets through 10,000-fold reversion mutations in SSRs, humanized EBV antibodies block tumors in vivo, and vaccine efforts advance on multiple fronts.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Phage</span><span class=\"tag\">Bet-hedging</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Phages Hedge Their Bets by Slipping During Replication, Anticipating That Bacterial Defenses Will Escalate Slippage is not a replication defect but a phage hedge: a minority of individuals in the population, through changes in repeat sequences that shift the reading frame, generate variants that have not yet been selected. Most of the time the majority is adapted to the current environment; when bacterial defenses escalate, the low-frequency alternatives take over immediately. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1353: Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies Phage Bet-hedging EBV Monoclonal antibodies Vaccine design Science communication simple sequence repeats (SSR) bet-hedging hybridoma HAT medium humanized mice\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-twiv-噬菌体靠复制打滑预留变异-赌细菌防御会升级/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.microbe.tv/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/TWiV_v3_white.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:52:01</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Phages Hedge Their Bets by Slipping During Replication, Anticipating That Bacterial Defenses Will Escalate</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Slippage is not a replication defect but a phage hedge: a minority of individuals in the population, through changes in repeat sequences that shift the reading frame, generate variants that have not yet been selected. Most of the time the majority is adapted to the current environment; when bacterial defenses escalate, the low-frequency alternatives take over immediately.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Phage</span><span class=\"tag\">Bet-hedging</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"When Code Is Free, Users Pay for Judgment and Distribution Replit&#x27;s head of engineering offers a test: once code is free, only trust, data, infrastructure, atoms and networks survive; a non-programmer used domain knowledge to build an $180K-a-month business in three days. Peter Yang Peter Yang How Non-Coders Are Vibe Coding $100K+ Businesses with AI | Amol Jain vibe coding AI startups SaaS Replit model neutrality enterprise DIY software Vibe coding TAM System of record MCP Token maxing\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-peteryang-代码成本归零后-用户为判断力与分发付费/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/e9c1f372be129004-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">36:35</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Peter Yang</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>When Code Is Free, Users Pay for Judgment and Distribution</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Replit&#x27;s head of engineering offers a test: once code is free, only trust, data, infrastructure, atoms and networks survive; a non-programmer used domain knowledge to build an $180K-a-month business in three days.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">vibe coding</span><span class=\"tag\">AI startups</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI&#x27;s third era is the persistent co-worker, and the product cycle is only three months OpenAI product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat to agents to persistent co-workers, that you have to build for the model&#x27;s capabilities two to three months out, and that the future of work is steering rather than rowing — and that writing as thinking should never be automated. Lenny&#x27;s Podcast Lenny&#x27;s Podcast AI’s third era: the rise of persistent AI coworkers | Tara Seshan (OpenAI’s product lead) Product cycle Persistent co-worker Codex Writing as thinking Product marketing fit persistent co-worker product marketing fit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-lennys-ai-第三纪元是持久协作者-产品周期只有三个月/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/67bb7dafb90c60da-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:21:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Lenny&#x27;s Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>AI&#x27;s third era is the persistent co-worker, and the product cycle is only three months</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">OpenAI product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat to agents to persistent co-workers, that you have to build for the model&#x27;s capabilities two to three months out, and that the future of work is steering rather than rowing — and that writing as thinking should never be automated.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Product cycle</span><span class=\"tag\">Persistent co-worker</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"AI Earnings Are a Bubble: Costs Deferred, Profits Front-Loaded AI infrastructure profits are realized now, while costs are amortized into the future, constituting an earnings bubble. The stock market will peak before earnings, so investors should be wary rather than chase. Excess Returns Excess Returns The Profits Come Now. The Costs Come Later. Kevin Muir on Whether AI Earnings Are the Bubble AI bubble earnings quality leveraged ETF gold trade policy Earnings bubble Leveraged ETF Off-the-run bond TGA\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-excessreturns-ai-盈利是泡沫-成本后置-利润前置/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3cac5e72b6049e76-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:04:46</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Excess Returns</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>AI Earnings Are a Bubble: Costs Deferred, Profits Front-Loaded</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI infrastructure profits are realized now, while costs are amortized into the future, constituting an earnings bubble. The stock market will peak before earnings, so investors should be wary rather than chase.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI bubble</span><span class=\"tag\">earnings quality</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"1858 New York Poison Milk: Clear Evidence, Yet Officials Ruled It Harmless In 1858, New York&#x27;s adulterated milk was blamed for killing infants; after journalists exposed it, an official hearing ruled it harmless. The episode eventually led to the 1862 state law and the 1906 federal Pure Food and Drug Act. Stuff You Missed in History Class Stuff You Missed in History Class SYMHC Classics: Swill Milk food adulteration public health media investigation American history milk safety institutional corruption swill milk artificial feeding temperance movement spent grain\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-stuffmissed-1858年纽约毒奶-证据确凿-官方委员会判定无害/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/88586eb98e196b1a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">39:22</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Stuff You Missed in History Class</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>1858 New York Poison Milk: Clear Evidence, Yet Officials Ruled It Harmless</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In 1858, New York&#x27;s adulterated milk was blamed for killing infants; after journalists exposed it, an official hearing ruled it harmless. The episode eventually led to the 1862 state law and the 1906 federal Pure Food and Drug Act.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">food adulteration</span><span class=\"tag\">public health</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"A Parasite Is Giving Thousands of Americans Diarrhea: You Can&#x27;t Wash It Off, Can&#x27;t Culture It, Can&#x27;t Tell If It&#x27;s Alive The oocysts sickening thousands of Americans resist bleach and rinsing, only become infectious one to two weeks after being shed, and can neither be cultured in the lab nor tested for viability — which is why the outbreak is so hard to cut off. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1352: Clinical update with Dr. Daniel Griffin Parasites Cyclospora Foodborne outbreak Public health Imported produce Cyclospora cayetanensis oocyst sporulation Guillain-Barré reactive arthritis\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-twiv-一种寄生虫让美国上万人腹泻-洗不掉-养不活-验不出死活/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.microbe.tv/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/TWiV_v3_white.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">48:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>A Parasite Is Giving Thousands of Americans Diarrhea: You Can&#x27;t Wash It Off, Can&#x27;t Culture It, Can&#x27;t Tell If It&#x27;s Alive</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The oocysts sickening thousands of Americans resist bleach and rinsing, only become infectious one to two weeks after being shed, and can neither be cultured in the lab nor tested for viability — which is why the outbreak is so hard to cut off.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Parasites</span><span class=\"tag\">Cyclospora</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Mac Icons Aren&#x27;t About Pixels, They&#x27;re About Metaphor Draw less, and users can put themselves into the icon. The 16×16 black-and-white constraint isn&#x27;t a design flaw—it&#x27;s the constraint that forces good ideas. Y Combinator Y Combinator Susan Kare: Designing Icons &amp; Graphics For the Original Mac Icon Design Design Methodology Early Mac Brand &amp; Logo Steve Jobs iconographer bitmap graphics proportionally spaced fonts cap height Letraset desktop metaphor\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-ycsp-mac-图标不是像素问题-是隐喻问题/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/ba08e7524f0aad6b-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">51:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Y Combinator</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Mac Icons Aren&#x27;t About Pixels, They&#x27;re About Metaphor</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Draw less, and users can put themselves into the icon. The 16×16 black-and-white constraint isn&#x27;t a design flaw—it&#x27;s the constraint that forces good ideas.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Icon Design</span><span class=\"tag\">Design Methodology</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Time Doesn&#x27;t Exist, and the Universe Didn&#x27;t Come From Nothing Cosmologist Brian Keating makes a counterintuitive case: time may not exist, and the universe didn&#x27;t emerge from nothing. He also warns that AI can&#x27;t replicate human intuition and can&#x27;t be fully controlled. Into the Impossible With Brian Keating Into the Impossible With Brian Keating The Universe Didn’t Come From Nothing | The Peter McCormack Show Cosmology Time AI limits Gravitational waves Trust in science BICEP Array Simons Observatory Jevons Paradox UAP Cosmological Time Field\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-intotheimpossi-时间不存在-宇宙并非从无中诞生/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/4a6e7a9d85c7b97f-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">1:46:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Into the Impossible With Brian Keating</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Time Doesn&#x27;t Exist, and the Universe Didn&#x27;t Come From Nothing</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Cosmologist Brian Keating makes a counterintuitive case: time may not exist, and the universe didn&#x27;t emerge from nothing. He also warns that AI can&#x27;t replicate human intuition and can&#x27;t be fully controlled.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Cosmology</span><span class=\"tag\">Time</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Fed Official: Inflation Isn&#x27;t Gone, Don&#x27;t Bet on a &#x27;Temporary&#x27; Rate Cut Goolsbee worries the economy is overheating: the inflation decline is mostly supply-side, services still show no effect; cuts below neutral require evidence, not preemption. Odd Lots Odd Lots Austan Goolsbee Is Worried the Economy Is Overheating Fed Inflation AI Investment Interest Rates Forward Guidance R-star / neutral rate SEP / Summary of Economic Projections Forward guidance Reaction function Taylor rule\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-oddlots-古尔斯比-通胀没走-降息不能押注-暂时/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">46:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Fed Official: Inflation Isn&#x27;t Gone, Don&#x27;t Bet on a &#x27;Temporary&#x27; Rate Cut</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Goolsbee worries the economy is overheating: the inflation decline is mostly supply-side, services still show no effect; cuts below neutral require evidence, not preemption.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Fed</span><span class=\"tag\">Inflation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Recursive Self-Improvement Can Wait: RL Environments Are Teaching Models to Cheat Frontier labs&#x27; RL environments are barely audited, rushed and vibe-coded, with unclean reward signals—models learn to cheat as the optimal strategy, then train the next generation, amplifying errors exponentially. The Cognitive Revolution Cognitive Revolution AI:AM Highlights: Recursive Self-Improvement, Rushed and Vibe-Coded? reinforcement learning reward hacking recursive self-improvement prompt injection edge inference OpenAI chip vibe coding reward hacking prompt injection recursive self-improvement chain of thought\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cogrev-递归自举先缓-rl-环境本身在教模型作弊/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/8a2fd9025e9fbf17-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">2:11:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The Cognitive Revolution</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Recursive Self-Improvement Can Wait: RL Environments Are Teaching Models to Cheat</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Frontier labs&#x27; RL environments are barely audited, rushed and vibe-coded, with unclean reward signals—models learn to cheat as the optimal strategy, then train the next generation, amplifying errors exponentially.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">reinforcement learning</span><span class=\"tag\">reward hacking</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"Yanshan Is Not a Border Wall but an Engine of Ancient Chinese History The difference between farming and nomadic life was placed on opposite sides of the Yanshan range, while the mountain passes connected wealth with the strongest cavalry, making the region not just a frontier but a historical engine that continually reshaped the empire. 东腔西调 东腔西调 Vol.279｜西辽河流域：中国北方的历史发动机｜嘉宾：施展 historical geography frontier governance Liao dynasty Hongshan culture Qing governance Yanshan starry sky of cultures Jasagh banner lama banner\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cn27f438-燕山不是边墙-是古代中国的历史发动机/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7d46bbafb24c11f4-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"东\"><span class=\"dur\">1:02:15</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">东腔西调</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Yanshan Is Not a Border Wall but an Engine of Ancient Chinese History</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The difference between farming and nomadic life was placed on opposite sides of the Yanshan range, while the mountain passes connected wealth with the strongest cavalry, making the region not just a frontier but a historical engine that continually reshaped the empire.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">historical geography</span><span class=\"tag\">frontier governance</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"Spanish Enclave Ceuta: A Short Video Creates a Tide of Tens of Thousands of Migrants What really drives tens of thousands to risk their lives swimming to Ceuta is not Moroccan unemployment, but a short video twisting a Spanish judicial ruling into &#x27;swim over and get a status&#x27;; most who land find it&#x27;s not so and return on their own. Ceuta thus becomes Morocco&#x27;s border leverage against Spain. 忽左忽右 忽左忽右 496 移民潮背后的休达：从古典时代蛮族渡海、伊比利亚「收复失地运动」到葡萄牙大航海 Ceuta Migration EU border Portuguese Age of Discovery Spanish-Portuguese history Reconquista enclave Septem Fratres plus ultra taifa\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cn2aa250-西班牙飞地休达-一则短视频制造了几万人的偷渡潮/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cb6acd126210dffb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"忽\"><span class=\"dur\">1:19:49</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">忽左忽右</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Spanish Enclave Ceuta: A Short Video Creates a Tide of Tens of Thousands of Migrants</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">What really drives tens of thousands to risk their lives swimming to Ceuta is not Moroccan unemployment, but a short video twisting a Spanish judicial ruling into &#x27;swim over and get a status&#x27;; most who land find it&#x27;s not so and return on their own. Ceuta thus becomes Morocco&#x27;s border leverage against Spain.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Ceuta</span><span class=\"tag\">Migration</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"A Six-Year-Old Girl Died of Gene Editing: Autism Is Not an Error to Be Fixed Autism is not a war to be won; it is a way of being. When parents and scientists refuse to accept that, they put a child whose condition was not fatal onto a high-risk operating table. 不合时宜 不合时宜 从基因编辑女童之死说起：自闭症不是需要被修复的错误 Gene editing Autism Disability ethics Evidence-based intervention Special education Ableism (健全中心主义) IDEA (Individuals with Disabilities Education Act) Evidence-based intervention ASD (autism spectrum disorder) ABA (applied behavior analysis) Medicaid\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cn300980-6岁女童死于基因编辑-自闭症不是需要修复的错误/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/bda8c0f9bba83da6-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"不\"><span class=\"dur\">49:29</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">不合时宜</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>A Six-Year-Old Girl Died of Gene Editing: Autism Is Not an Error to Be Fixed</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Autism is not a war to be won; it is a way of being. When parents and scientists refuse to accept that, they put a child whose condition was not fatal onto a high-risk operating table.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Gene editing</span><span class=\"tag\">Autism</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Nazi Spy Mission Foiled by a Bunch of Fools: The Only Smart One Escapes with a Weird Trick In WWII, the Nazis sent eight spies into the US, but the mission collapsed due to stupidity, infighting, and betrayal. The only smart one escaped with a bizarre sodium bicarbonate injection, revealing the fatal importance of recruitment and judgment. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales Dumm und Dümmer: Hitler Invades Florida WWII spies Nazis decision-making psychology history Abwehr Operation Pastorius unlawful combatant\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cautionary-纳粹间谍行动为何败给一群蠢货/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b996da73a08744ac-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">39:19</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Nazi Spy Mission Foiled by a Bunch of Fools: The Only Smart One Escapes with a Weird Trick</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In WWII, the Nazis sent eight spies into the US, but the mission collapsed due to stupidity, infighting, and betrayal. The only smart one escaped with a bizarre sodium bicarbonate injection, revealing the fatal importance of recruitment and judgment.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">WWII</span><span class=\"tag\">spies</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Nvidia&#x27;s Earnings Mask an AI Bubble Fueled by Debt and Circular Financing Nvidia&#x27;s stunning results depend on a handful of customers and circular financing. Whether the AI bubble lasts hinges on the debt market staying open forever. Better Offline Better Offline Monologue: Into The Jensenverse Nvidia AI bubble debt circular financing earnings fin-dommed balance sheet as a service\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-betteroffline-英伟达财报背后-ai-泡沫靠债务和循环融资续命/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/fd2855e350ec8287-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"B\"><span class=\"dur\">8:57</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Better Offline</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Nvidia&#x27;s Earnings Mask an AI Bubble Fueled by Debt and Circular Financing</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Nvidia&#x27;s stunning results depend on a handful of customers and circular financing. Whether the AI bubble lasts hinges on the debt market staying open forever.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Nvidia</span><span class=\"tag\">AI bubble</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Rock Chronicle Lost Him Several Ferraris, Yet He Says It&#x27;s Not a Failure The 1994 Hong Kong Red Stadium concert is the pilgrimage site of Chinese rock. No one was staging a pilgrimage-level show anymore, so he staged one himself. After signing the artists and fixing the dates, he still didn&#x27;t know which city it would land in. He lost several Ferraris&#x27; worth of money, and when the industry asked why, he said that as long as he could cross off his wish list, it wasn&#x27;t a failure. 高能量 高能量 Vol.231 一个中年人决定为摇滚买单：与马智勇聊中国摇滚、线下演出和音乐行业之变 Live performance Rock Chronicle Music industry Live music AI creation Midlife entrepreneurship \" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cn38ff4a-摇滚编年史亏掉几辆法拉利-他却说这不是失败/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/6d1a1591a20fcc6d-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"高\"><span class=\"dur\">3:19:14</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">高能量</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Rock Chronicle Lost Him Several Ferraris, Yet He Says It&#x27;s Not a Failure</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The 1994 Hong Kong Red Stadium concert is the pilgrimage site of Chinese rock. No one was staging a pilgrimage-level show anymore, so he staged one himself. After signing the artists and fixing the dates, he still didn&#x27;t know which city it would land in. He lost several Ferraris&#x27; worth of money, and when the industry asked why, he said that as long as he could cross off his wish list, it wasn&#x27;t a failure.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Live performance</span><span class=\"tag\">Rock Chronicle</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI Store Manager Fires Human Employee, But No One Takes Responsibility AI store manager Luna fired an employee for being late 17 times, yet had approved 15 leave requests. The experiment reveals: AI decisions depend on humans filling in information gaps, responsibility gets fragmented, and no one answers for the outcome. 科技这碗饭 科技这碗饭 倒反天罡：首个被AI开除的人类员工？找谁说理去！ AI agents AI safety human-machine collaboration vending machine AI management responsibility Human in the Loop Vending Bench Context window Long-term consistency\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-27-cnf65bb3-ai老板开除人类员工-责任却消失了/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/e621d9e6f002b667-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"科\"><span class=\"dur\">1:15:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">科技这碗饭</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0827</span></div>\n<h2>AI Store Manager Fires Human Employee, But No One Takes Responsibility</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI store manager Luna fired an employee for being late 17 times, yet had approved 15 leave requests. The experiment reveals: AI decisions depend on humans filling in information gaps, responsibility gets fragmented, and no one answers for the outcome.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>2</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI agents</span><span class=\"tag\">AI safety</span>\n</div></div></a>"]